   "id": "b3",
   "function": "explanation",
   "scene_type": "zlx_chart",
   "spoken": "The engineering lecture splits diesel combustion into four phases. First the ignition delay. Then everything that has already mixed burns at once: the premixed phase. According to the lecture, this steep pressure rise is also what makes a diesel sound the way it does. Watch the steep spike in the curve. First the delay, then the burst.",
